  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Image asset data\n- Added FileData for image bytes or Base64String values, with Bytes and Base64 accessors.\n- Breaking: ImageAsset now accepts FileData instead of a base64 string. Pass bytes directly or wrap encoded data in new Base64String(value). Replace asset.Base64 with asset.FileData.Base64.\n- ImageAsset.FromByteArray is obsolete; use new ImageAsset(name, format, bytes) instead.\n- Updated image asset and request tests for the new API, resolving test project compilation errors.\n\nUsage pricing and aggregation\n- Added JevPrice with decimal rates per million input and output tokens; the output rate defaults to zero.\n- Added Usage.CalculateCost, Usage.Zero, Usage.Add, and IEnumerable<Usage>.SumUsage(). Addition and aggregation sum input and output counts independently without changing operands; an empty sequence sums to zero.\n\nSource-generated query execution\n- Generated Execute methods now accept IJevRunner instead of concrete JevRunner, supporting interface-typed runners and alternative implementations while preserving cancellation-token forwarding and typed response wrappers.\n- Updated source-generator test contracts and regression coverage for interface-based execution.\n\nBreaking change\n- Usage is now a readonly record struct instead of a record class. It has value semantics and a zero-valued default; callers relying on null or reference identity must update their code.",
